{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/96726.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS ESS-457B67: Pedestal base from a Roman statuette, top view"]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["statuetta"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (statuetta)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["43-410 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Essex (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["Incomplete, cast copper-alloy Roman pedestal base which would originally have held a copper-alloy figurine. The main platform of the pedestal base is square in plan and flat in section. It has a down turned flanged rim, set at 90 degrees, of which three sides are damaged. At each corner of the undamaged side is a globular foot, the other two feet are entirely missing. Extending vertically from the centre of the base is a hexagonal column, with an integrally moulded hexagonal band to top and bottom. Above the upper most band sits an integral, flat circular platform, upon which the figurine would have been positioned. The column is hollow. The original surface of the object is much abraded.…"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["ESS-457B67"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["96726"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: Colchester Museums, Caroline McDonald, 2005-05-25 10:53:56, CC BY-SA 2.0 ; Colchester Museums, Caroline McDonald, 2005-05-25 10:53:56, CC BY-SA 4.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/96726","type":"Text","label":{"none":["PAS ESS-457B